CYBER SECURITY

Cyber security is the practice of protecting computers, networks, applications, and data from unauthorized access and digital threats.

COMMON CYBER THREATS

Phishing is a technique where attackers attempt to trick users into providing sensitive information.

Malware is malicious software designed to damage systems, steal information, or perform unauthorized activities.

Strong passwords help protect user accounts from unauthorized access.

Two-factor authentication provides an additional layer of security by requiring another verification step.

DATA PROTECTION

Organizations should protect sensitive information through access controls, encryption, secure backups, and regular security updates.

USER AWARENESS

Users play an important role in cyber security. They should avoid suspicious links, use strong unique passwords, keep software updated, and be careful when sharing personal information online.

Cyber security is important because modern organizations depend heavily on computers, networks, and digital information.